1
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
(Blossom Through the Cloud)

2
00:01:35,001 --> 00:01:37,960
(Adapted from the novel on JJWXC, "Landing on My Heart", by Qiao Yao)

3
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:54,560
Be careful!

4
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:56,599
Mom, the other kids all say...

5
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:57,600
that you're the best.

6
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,280
How so?

7
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,720
Because you never scold me,

8
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:01,920
and you never hit me.

9
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,176
Even if I don't do well on exams,

10
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,200
you don't get mad.

11
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,560
I still hope you do well.

12
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,400
Please try to get a better grade next time, okay?

13
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:12,000
We'll talk about that when the next exam comes.

14
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,400
When is the next time?

15
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,440
The next time after the next time!

16
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,000
You little rascal.

17
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:18,440
I'm going to catch you!

18
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:43,280
(Episode 11: Happy Birthday x 3)

19
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Come in, Xiao Ruan.

20
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,016
Welcome. It's your first time here, right?

21
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,040
Come this way.

22
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:54,200
Welcome to Hengshi's executive floor.

23
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:57,120
This is where Mr. Fu and the rest of us work.

24
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,640
Come, let's walk further in. I'll show you around.

25
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,680
This is the pantry.

26
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,520
Usually, people come here to have coffee and take a break.

27
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,520
The staff working here...

28
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,280
are all from the President's Office.

29
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:15,480
And this is Mr. Fu's office.

30
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:29,160
Didn't check your phone?

31
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:32,720
No. What's wrong?

32
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:34,360
I have another meeting.

33
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:35,600
Wait a moment.

34
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,200
Here, Xiao Ruan.

35
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:48,240
Have some water.

36
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,160
Mr. Fu, everyone is here.

37
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:57,280
When it's over, I'll take you to dinner.

38
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:15,720
Wait a minute.

39
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,760
Why should I wait just because you said so?

40
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:21,880
And taking me to dinner?

41
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:24,080
Do I not have a mouth to feed myself...
or legs to walk away?

42
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,520
Besides,

43
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:28,920
are you and I on good enough terms to eat together?

44
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:33,280
It's probably not about work.

45
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,880
(WeChat, Fu Ming Yu)

46
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:38,960
(Fu Ming Yu: I'm back.)

47
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:40,800
He can just come back.

48
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:42,640
Why notify me?

49
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:46,480
This time, Mr. Fu...

50
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:48,640
really earned some major points.

51
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:50,520
If he hadn't been there,

52
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,936
you would've been in trouble today.

53
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:52,960
Yeah.
A hero saving the damsel.

54
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:55,320
I think he has a chance.

55
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:56,360
Even an unreliable guy like him...

56
00:04:56,361 --> 00:04:57,920
can have such a considerate side.

57
00:04:58,520 --> 00:04:59,800
Sorry for the trouble, everyone.

58
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:02,480
This Fu Ming Yu...

59
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:04,799
just came back from Ma'ao...

60
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,800
with another woman,

61
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,440
and now he's rushing to ask me out.

62
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,360
Ms. Ruan,

63
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:17,600
where are you going?

64
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:18,680
Home.

65
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,720
Tell Mr. Fu...

66
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:21,680
to eat by himself.

67
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,400
Where is she?

68
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:39,600
Where is Ruan Si Xian?

69
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:41,080
Ms. Ruan said...

70
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,680
she had something to do and went home.

71
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:43,960
Did she say what it was?

72
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,600
She just said...

73
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,880
you should eat by yourself.

74
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:03,960
Hello, "Captain" Ruan.

75
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:05,760
West Chamber Banquet is at your service.

76
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,040
You...

77
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,240
You all...

78
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,520
Who told you to come?

79
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:14,760
I didn't order any service.

80
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:15,800
- This... - Hello.

81
00:06:15,801 --> 00:06:17,039
- You... - Mr. Fu arranged this for you.

82
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:18,199
It's an in-home cooking service.

83
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:19,760
Let's hurry up and get to work.

84
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:22,160
I... Wait!

85
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:24,079
- What are you doing? - Didn't we agree?

86
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:26,120
We would have dinner together after I got off work.

87
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:30,920
Aren't you going to invite me in?

88
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:36,440
An An.

89
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,720
An An.

90
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Are you busy?

91
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:41,720
I'm...

92
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:43,320
organizing photos.

93
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,240
What's up? Let's have some fruit and chat.

94
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:48,600
About what? I'm really busy right now.

95
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:51,440
All right. I'll let you get back to it.

96
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Well,

97
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,120
I'll get going.

98
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:57,280
Mom.

99
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:01,720
Let's chat, come on.

100
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:06,320
So how was it?

101
00:07:06,321 --> 00:07:08,040
Did you have fun in Ma'ao?

102
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:09,560
Seven days.

103
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:12,120
I was in Ma'ao for seven whole days.

104
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:14,640
He didn't even have time to have a single meal with me.

105
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:16,560
I don't believe he was really that busy.

106
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:18,679
I feel like taking me to Ma'ao...

107
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:20,920
was just another task on his to-do list.

108
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:23,680
Maybe he really was busy.

109
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:25,080
Look at your dad.

110
00:07:25,081 --> 00:07:27,121
He's always so busy that he's constantly on the go.

111
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:28,920
Anyway, I'm pretty annoyed.

112
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:30,840
However,

113
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:33,000
the trip wasn't a total waste.

114
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:36,680
I'm absolutely certain of one thing now.

115
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:38,160
I, Zheng You An,

116
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,000
do not like Fu Ming Yu.

117
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,679
If you want to know to what extent,

118
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:44,680
it's that I 100 percent do not like him.

119
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:46,880
Help me talk to Dad too.

120
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:48,640
Tell him to give up on that idea.

121
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:55,560
What are you laughing at?

122
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,599
Then why did you follow Fu Ming Yu around...

123
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,960
all the time when you were little?

124
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,279
I was just a kid then.

125
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,640
What did I know?

126
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,320
It's all because of you adults.

127
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,696
You teased me about it every day.

128
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:06,840
You made me believe that I really liked him.

129
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,336
I've been mistaken for so many years.

130
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,360
But this time in Ma'ao,

131
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:12,200
I finally set things straight...

132
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,400
and found out the truth.

133
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:16,760
All right, now that you know the truth,

134
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
are you happy?

135
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:21,760
The two artists...

136
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:23,640
are obsessed with art again.

137
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:24,840
Even if you're obsessed with art,

138
00:08:24,841 --> 00:08:26,321
you should still have a meal with me.

139
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,040
That's right.
In this big world,

140
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,680
eating is the most important thing.

141
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,879
Right. I'll answer your question while I'm at it.

142
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:37,079
I feel refreshed now.

143
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,320
I'm in a great mood.

144
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:45,040
What has gotten into her?

145
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:47,480
As I said before,

146
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:50,080
the most important thing is for our child to be happy.

147
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,120
Old Zheng.

148
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:53,280
What did you make?

149
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:55,519
Sweet and sour pork ribs.

150
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:56,520
- Go on. - Let's go.

151
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:57,680
- Let's eat. - Let's go.

152
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,480
- Enjoy your meal. - Enjoy your meal.

153
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:38,760
Mr. Fu, we'll get going now.
Okay, thank you for your hard work.

154
00:09:39,761 --> 00:09:40,840
You're welcome.

155
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:48,760
Please.

156
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,280
How extravagant.

157
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:53,240
Even though you own this place,

158
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,960
you can't be so overbearing and unscrupulous.

159
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:57,760
You don't like it?

160
00:09:57,761 --> 00:09:59,639
If you don't like it, we can eat out next time.

161
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:01,199
Is that the point?

162
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,400
Who wants to eat out with you?

163
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:03,680
What I'm saying is,

164
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:06,159
you just came back from Ma'ao with your girlfriend.

165
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:07,760
Why are you asking me out to a meal now?

166
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
She's not my girlfriend.

167
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:11,280
Who would believe that?

168
00:10:11,281 --> 00:10:13,576
She's the daughter of the chairman of a company I work with.

169
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:15,200
She had work in Ma'ao,

170
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:17,559
but since she couldn't find a suitable flight,

171
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:18,800
she hitched a ride on my plane.

172
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:32,440
Please have a seat.

173
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:40,360
How did you know I like Sichuan and Hunan cuisine?

174
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,536
It's not hard to deduce the preferences...

175
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:44,880
of someone who eats spicy food...

176
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,280
while having a stomachache.

177
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Try it.

178
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:53,520
Aren't you eating?

179
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,600
You first.

180
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:05,960
It's actually quite good.

181
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:42,720
You clearly can't handle spicy food.

182
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:48,760
- So... - So...

183
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:53,640
(Zheng You An)

184
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:05,520
What were you going to say just now?

185
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:10,160
What do you think of Zheng You An?

186
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,160
If Zheng You An hadn't made that call...

187
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,559
what would you have asked?

188
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:15,840
If she hadn't called,

189
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:17,360
that's exactly what I wanted to ask.

190
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:19,960
Fine.

191
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:21,560
Then I'll explain it one more time.

192
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:23,799
She's the daughter of the chairman of a company I work with.

193
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:25,040
Her parents and mine...

194
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:26,400
are on good terms,

195
00:12:26,401 --> 00:12:27,481
so we see each other often.

196
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:28,920
That's all there is to it.

197
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:30,520
Then what kind of person is she?

198
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:32,600
She and I...

199
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,240
basically grew up together.

200
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,320
Later, she went to study abroad.

201
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:38,600
We rarely met after she left.

202
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:39,840
In the past five years,

203
00:12:39,841 --> 00:12:41,639
we've seen each other no more than five times.

204
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:43,336
We haven't even spoken 20 sentences to each other.

205
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,239
As for what kind of person she is now, I'm not sure.

206
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,240
But...

207
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:47,920
I have no relationship with her.

208
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:51,520
Fine.

209
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:52,920
Forget it if you don't know.

210
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:58,880
I'm so sorry.

211
00:12:58,881 --> 00:12:59,919
My car broke down on the way.

212
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:00,920
I had to push it here.

213
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:02,399
And I was at the security office registering for ages.

214
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:03,559
I'm sorry I'm late.

215
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:04,640
It's okay.

216
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:07,000
Thank you for your hard work.

217
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:09,080
It's hot out. Have some water.

218
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:10,240
- It's fine. - Thank you.

219
00:13:10,241 --> 00:13:11,280
- Thank you. - Thank you.

220
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,320
Did you order takeout?

221
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:31,000
You were quite nice to the delivery guy just now.

222
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:32,480
If you were a delivery guy,

223
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:33,600
I'd be nice to you too.

224
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:35,160
I can't help it.

225
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:36,680
I sympathize with the working class.

226
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:04,360
These dishes...

227
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:05,960
taste pretty good.

228
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,120
No rush.

229
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:08,600
You can eat more.

230
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,040
I have a meeting later,

231
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,040
so I have to head back to the office.

232
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:34,600
Xuan.

233
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:44,840
What's wrong?

234
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:48,480
Nothing.

235
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,440
I'm just a little tired.

236
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:52,840
Are you flying these next few days?

237
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:57,680
Perfect. Try our new cocktail.

238
00:14:58,360 --> 00:14:59,360
Sunset Boulevard.

239
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:01,320
You're the first one to try it.

240
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:14,280
- How is it? - It's sweet.

241
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:16,759
Don't underestimate it though.

242
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:18,840
It's just as strong as a Long Island Iced Tea.

243
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:23,960
Is something on your mind?

244
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:26,520
No.

245
00:15:26,640 --> 00:15:28,200
Excuse me. Can I see the menu?

246
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:29,520
Coming!

247
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:31,920
Wait for me in the courtyard.

248
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:33,080
I'll be right there.

249
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,280
You drank the whole thing?

250
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:17,200
Are you fine?
I'm okay.

251
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,360
It's just like juice.

252
00:16:26,680 --> 00:16:27,680
Tell me the truth.

253
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:30,240
Did your mother come to see you again?

254
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:34,480
No.

255
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:39,040
That's good.

256
00:16:40,320 --> 00:16:41,560
Then let's toast.

257
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:38,760
Are you hungry?

258
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:40,480
I'm not hungry.

259
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,520
I think I'm a little hungry.

260
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:46,200
I wonder what your dad is cooking for us.

261
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,160
Be careful.

262
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,480
Watch where you're walking.

263
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:53,120
There's a bug there. I'm scared.

264
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:55,320
Don't be scared.

265
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:56,400
Mom is here.

266
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:25,280
Why were you drinking?

267
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,920
I'm in a bad mood.

268
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:31,720
What's wrong?

269
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:34,280
I'm just...

270
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:36,320
in a bad mood.

271
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:40,360
Still angry?

272
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:44,920
So you're angry,

273
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:47,536
and that's why you haven't replied to my messages.

274
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:49,240
I just didn't want to reply.

275
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:52,560
It's my fault.

276
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:54,800
I was on a business trip for so long,

277
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:57,160
and I didn't even send you a single message.

278
00:18:57,840 --> 00:18:59,120
I don't care if you text or not.

279
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,680
Do you hate me that much?

280
00:19:03,080 --> 00:19:04,080
I'm not that bad, am I?

281
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:06,480
Not really.

282
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:08,960
Actually,

283
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,960
you're quite nice sometimes.

284
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:13,040
- I... - But...

285
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,360
Sometimes,

286
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:16,360
I really want to kick you...

287
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:17,480
all the way to Trisolaris.

288
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:25,840
Why are you so angry?

289
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:28,320
Is it because of Zheng You An?

290
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:30,680
If that's the case,

291
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,760
I won't go out with her alone next time.

292
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:35,600
Okay?

293
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:37,600
If I'm mad at Zheng You An,

294
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:39,080
what does that have to do with you?

295
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:42,320
You're so jealous.

296
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:43,600
How can it not be about me?

297
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,680
You don't think...

298
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,240
I'm jealous of Zheng You An...

299
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:54,040
because of you, do you?

300
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:57,120
You...

301
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:59,840
Were you a hot air balloon in your past life?

302
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:01,176
Because your ego is so inflated.

303
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,280
Who's jealous of you?

304
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:09,840
I don't want to walk anymore.

305
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:13,920
I have an inflated ego?

306
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:14,600
Who are you looking for?

307
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:17,120
Where's Ruan Ruan?

308
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:18,720
She left.

309
00:21:18,721 --> 00:21:20,921
Why are you here today instead of going to see Lu Ming?

310
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:22,120
Him?

311
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:23,720
He went out to have fun.

312
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Perfect.

313
00:21:27,001 --> 00:21:28,720
I think while Ruan Ruan isn't here,

314
00:21:28,760 --> 00:21:31,080
we should discuss how to celebrate her birthday this year.

315
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:34,040
But doesn't she skip her birthday?

316
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:37,840
That's just an excuse she uses.

317
00:21:38,080 --> 00:21:39,480
Because every year on her birthday,

318
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:40,880
her mother comes to see her.

319
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:43,519
She says she wants nothing to do with her mother.

320
00:21:43,520 --> 00:21:45,640
But look at her. Does she look like she doesn't care?

321
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:46,960
How about this?

322
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:48,920
Let's take her out this year.

323
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:50,296
If she doesn't see her mother,

324
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:51,720
maybe she'll have a happy birthday.

325
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:53,120
Then...

326
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,680
let's get a cake and flowers.

327
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,160
How about camping by the sea?

328
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:58,720
It's a plan!

329
00:21:58,840 --> 00:22:00,039
- Okay. - Then...

330
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:01,040
I'll get the cake.

331
00:22:01,041 --> 00:22:02,080
I'll get the flowers.

332
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:03,759
What about me?

333
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:04,839
You?

334
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:06,040
Just stay out of the way.

335
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:23,960
I need your fingerprint.

336
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:48,800
Careful.

337
00:23:09,600 --> 00:23:10,880
Are you still in a bad mood?

338
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,320
I am unhappy,

339
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:17,320
but it's none of your business.

340
00:23:17,360 --> 00:23:18,360
Do you understand?

341
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:21,120
Don't flatter yourself.

342
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:32,120
It's not because of me.

343
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:34,080
Why did you drink so much?

344
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,519
It's my mouth.

345
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:37,000
So what if I drink?

346
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:39,559
Is it any of your business?

347
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:40,999
Are you my boyfriend...

348
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:42,680
or my husband?

349
00:23:43,280 --> 00:23:44,680
How ridiculous.

350
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:02,680
I'm just so jealous of Zheng You An.

351
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:05,840
I'm so jealous of her.

352
00:24:08,760 --> 00:24:09,760
Jealous of what?

353
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:15,720
They aren't even related by blood,

354
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:19,400
but they can be together every day.

355
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:25,360
What are you talking about?

356
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:29,120
I'm her own,

357
00:24:31,920 --> 00:24:33,920
but she doesn't want me anymore.

358
00:24:43,800 --> 00:24:44,800
Who doesn't want you?

359
00:24:46,120 --> 00:24:47,440
My mom.

360
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:52,640
My mom abandoned me.

361
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:14,720
Why haven't you left yet?

362
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:16,600
You're drunk.

363
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:17,760
I brought you home.

364
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:19,320
You opened the door yourself.

365
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,800
Just because the door was open,

366
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:22,240
you let yourself in?

367
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:25,799
Banks have their doors open too.

368
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:27,360
Why don't you go rob one?

369
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:30,000
Ruan Si Xian, can't you talk to me nicely?

370
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:32,080
Are you leaving or not?

371
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:33,960
What if I don't?

372
00:25:34,720 --> 00:25:36,640
If you don't leave,

373
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:39,240
I'll send you...

374
00:25:39,760 --> 00:25:42,200
down in a free fall.

375
00:25:43,160 --> 00:25:44,480
You don't even need the elevator.

376
00:25:57,200 --> 00:25:58,200
- Hello? - Hello?

377
00:25:58,520 --> 00:25:59,560
This is Fu Ming Yu.

378
00:26:01,720 --> 00:26:02,720
Hello.

379
00:26:02,880 --> 00:26:05,240
Hello. Is Ruan Si Xian there?

380
00:26:05,800 --> 00:26:06,800
She's drunk.

381
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:08,400
I've brought her home.

382
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:09,480
Okay.

383
00:26:12,840 --> 00:26:15,120
I just wanted to confirm she's home safe.

384
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:19,280
Okay, thank you.

385
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:20,880
Wait, was that...

386
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:22,000
Fu Ming Yu?

387
00:26:23,120 --> 00:26:24,120
It was Fu Ming Yu.

388
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:27,280
- They... - Anyway, Ruan Ruan is drunk.

389
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:29,039
So they...

390
00:26:29,040 --> 00:26:30,040
And...

391
00:26:30,041 --> 00:26:31,199
Fu Ming Yu is at Ruan Ruan's place now.

392
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:32,200
No way!

393
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:33,359
- No! - It must be like that.

394
00:26:33,360 --> 00:26:34,599
It must be. That's it.

395
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:36,319
I really want to call her again.

396
00:26:36,320 --> 00:26:37,839
- No, you can't. - Don't disturb them.

397
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:38,879
Ruan Ruan...

398
00:26:38,880 --> 00:26:39,960
She has finally found love!

399
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:56,560
Let go of me.

400
00:26:57,080 --> 00:26:58,560
If you want to sleep, go to your bed.

401
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:01,120
Don't squeeze onto that small sofa.

402
00:27:16,480 --> 00:27:18,600
I'm her own daughter.

403
00:27:19,040 --> 00:27:20,760
But she didn't want me anymore.

404
00:27:53,360 --> 00:27:54,360
It's 11pm.

405
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:55,680
Are you going back to Huguang?

406
00:28:19,880 --> 00:28:21,480
Look into Ms. Dong's past.

407
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:23,120
Yes, sir.

408
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:34,960
- Mom. - Son, you're back.

409
00:28:36,320 --> 00:28:37,320
Son,

410
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:38,920
I'm unhappy today.

411
00:28:39,480 --> 00:28:40,480
What's wrong?

412
00:28:40,560 --> 00:28:42,360
Tell me, how can there be such a person?

413
00:28:44,320 --> 00:28:46,000
At tonight's private auction,

414
00:28:46,560 --> 00:28:47,879
everyone knew I was there...

415
00:28:47,880 --> 00:28:49,400
for Master Yue Sanlin's painting.

416
00:28:49,720 --> 00:28:51,040
I even brought the money.

417
00:28:51,240 --> 00:28:52,240
But when I got there,

418
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:55,800
the master's painting wasn't even among the auction items.

419
00:28:56,640 --> 00:28:58,759
- Do you know what happened? - What happened?

420
00:28:58,760 --> 00:28:59,839
(Bai Yang: Mr. Fu, I've found out.)

421
00:28:59,840 --> 00:29:01,960
Dong Xian pulled a fast one.

422
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:03,800
She had bought the painting beforehand!

423
00:29:04,320 --> 00:29:05,320
How awful.

424
00:29:05,800 --> 00:29:07,640
Mom, just buy another one.

425
00:29:08,600 --> 00:29:10,080
- I'll... - I'm going to make a call.

426
00:29:15,200 --> 00:29:16,719
You don't want to hear me nag.

427
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:18,320
You don't want to hear me complain.

428
00:29:19,440 --> 00:29:21,480
Making roast pork is better than raising a son.

429
00:29:21,800 --> 00:29:23,760
Collecting treasure is better than raising a son.

430
00:29:28,360 --> 00:29:29,360
Hello, Mr. Fu.

431
00:29:29,640 --> 00:29:31,679
- Get straight to the point. - Here's the story.

432
00:29:31,680 --> 00:29:34,176
Mr. Zheng and the current Mrs. Zheng are in their second marriage.

433
00:29:34,200 --> 00:29:35,400
Everyone knows this.

434
00:29:35,520 --> 00:29:37,879
Mr. Zheng's first wife passed away from illness...

435
00:29:37,880 --> 00:29:39,480
shortly after giving birth to Ms. Zheng.

436
00:29:39,720 --> 00:29:40,720
The current Mrs. Zheng...

437
00:29:41,080 --> 00:29:42,080
had a former husband,

438
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:44,120
but he passed away a long time ago.

439
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:45,880
Get to the point.

440
00:29:46,280 --> 00:29:47,280
The point is,

441
00:29:47,720 --> 00:29:49,080
Mrs. Zheng had a daughter before.

442
00:29:50,200 --> 00:29:51,200
It's Ruan Si Xian.

443
00:29:59,320 --> 00:30:00,320
I see.

444
00:30:06,240 --> 00:30:07,480
It's great that you could come.

445
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:14,760
What do you think of Zheng You An?

446
00:30:15,040 --> 00:30:17,679
If Zheng You An hadn't called, what would you have asked?

447
00:30:17,680 --> 00:30:19,239
If she hadn't called,

448
00:30:19,240 --> 00:30:20,560
that's what I would've asked too.

449
00:30:22,600 --> 00:30:24,360
I'm her own,

450
00:30:27,120 --> 00:30:29,320
yet she didn't want me anymore.

451
00:30:38,440 --> 00:30:40,120
I really was reading too much into things.

452
00:31:40,840 --> 00:31:41,840
Careful.

453
00:31:56,960 --> 00:31:57,960
Who is it?

454
00:31:59,440 --> 00:32:01,000
Hello. Here's your delivery. Enjoy.

455
00:32:30,520 --> 00:32:32,760
(Fu Ming Yu)

456
00:32:35,800 --> 00:32:37,360
I received the breakfast. Thank you.

457
00:32:41,840 --> 00:32:43,239
(Bian Xuan)

458
00:32:43,240 --> 00:32:45,296
Are you awake? I was afraid you would feel unwell if you overslept.

459
00:32:45,320 --> 00:32:46,440
I ordered breakfast for you.

460
00:32:46,600 --> 00:32:47,600
Remember to eat it.

461
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:53,200
It wasn't from him?

462
00:32:53,201 --> 00:32:55,120
(Fu Ming Yu, Recall Message)

463
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:56,199
(Ruan Si Xian: I received the breakfast. Thank you.)

464
00:32:56,200 --> 00:33:01,760
(The other user recalled a message.)

465
00:33:06,200 --> 00:33:07,200
It wasn't me.

466
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:08,800
Don't overthink it.

467
00:33:12,360 --> 00:33:13,760
I just sent it to the wrong person.

468
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:14,800
Sorry.

469
00:33:21,160 --> 00:33:22,160
"Oh"?

470
00:33:34,640 --> 00:33:36,320
Thanks to my besties for breakfast.

471
00:33:36,640 --> 00:33:37,640
Love you all.

472
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:38,720
Kisses.

473
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:42,400
I don't believe you.

474
00:33:45,200 --> 00:33:49,360
(Thanks to my besties for breakfast. Love you all. Kisses.)

475
00:33:49,680 --> 00:33:52,839
(You're here to see me again. Admit it. You like me.)

476
00:33:52,840 --> 00:33:53,960
You're here to see me again.

477
00:33:54,160 --> 00:33:55,160
Admit it.

478
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:56,200
You like me.

479
00:34:06,400 --> 00:34:07,519
(Employee Registration Form, Ruan Si Xian)

480
00:34:07,520 --> 00:34:10,480
(Birthdate: August 25, 1993)

481
00:34:13,680 --> 00:34:14,680
Bai Yang.

482
00:34:15,240 --> 00:34:17,360
Tomorrow, order a birthday cake for me.

483
00:34:18,760 --> 00:34:19,760
Got it. Don't worry.

484
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:21,000
Make it a nice one.

485
00:34:22,200 --> 00:34:23,200
Will do.

486
00:34:27,640 --> 00:34:28,640
Hello, everyone.

487
00:34:28,641 --> 00:34:30,600
Welcome to FM 93.7,

488
00:34:30,840 --> 00:34:32,000
Jiangcheng Sound of Music.

489
00:34:32,640 --> 00:34:33,640
Next, we'll bring you...

490
00:34:33,641 --> 00:34:34,800
today's weather forecast...

491
00:34:34,920 --> 00:34:36,160
and meteorological information.

492
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:38,240
There will be heavy rain in the city today.

493
00:34:38,280 --> 00:34:39,960
The high will be 28°C,

494
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:41,760
and the low will be 15°C.

495
00:34:42,240 --> 00:34:43,680
Please bring your rain gear.

496
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:47,760
The sun is so bright.

497
00:34:48,240 --> 00:34:50,240
It doesn't look like it's going to rain at all.

498
00:34:51,720 --> 00:34:53,080
The weather forecast these days...

499
00:34:53,480 --> 00:34:54,920
is getting more and more unreliable.

500
00:35:07,080 --> 00:35:08,960
Are these three orders duplicates?

501
00:35:10,520 --> 00:35:11,520
What do you mean?

502
00:35:11,640 --> 00:35:13,199
They all ordered the same cake.

503
00:35:13,200 --> 00:35:14,200
(Customer: Si Xiao Zhen, Item: Kids' Airplane Cream Cake)
They're not duplicates.

504
00:35:15,320 --> 00:35:16,880
The three buyers are all different.

505
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:18,999
The first two messages are also different.

506
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:20,280
They both wish "Happy Birthday".

507
00:35:20,520 --> 00:35:23,360
The third one wrote a whole letter.

508
00:35:24,600 --> 00:35:26,479
But it's obvious...

509
00:35:26,480 --> 00:35:28,080
they're all for the same person.

510
00:35:28,400 --> 00:35:30,200
Ruan Si Xian, Captain Ruan,

511
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:31,400
and Ruan Ruan.

512
00:35:32,040 --> 00:35:33,720
No, I have to check.

513
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:42,880
Hello?

514
00:35:43,560 --> 00:35:44,560
Hello.

515
00:35:44,880 --> 00:35:47,039
This is Big Cousin Cake and Bakery.

516
00:35:47,040 --> 00:35:48,200
I'm the "Big Cousin" here.

517
00:35:48,360 --> 00:35:51,800
Did you order a children's airplane cake from us?

518
00:35:52,080 --> 00:35:54,319
- That's right. - This is a cake for children.

519
00:35:54,320 --> 00:35:55,560
Are you sure you want this one?

520
00:35:56,280 --> 00:35:59,640
Yes. Could you make the little airplane look cuter?

521
00:35:59,840 --> 00:36:01,999
- Thank you. - I see the note here.

522
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:03,120
No peaches.

523
00:36:03,520 --> 00:36:05,600
Yes, that's right. Make sure not to add any peaches.

524
00:36:05,680 --> 00:36:07,000
She's allergic to them.

525
00:36:07,360 --> 00:36:08,360
Any other fruit is fine.

526
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:10,519
So the message on the cake should be,

527
00:36:10,520 --> 00:36:12,199
"Ruan Si Xian, Happy Birthday".

528
00:36:12,200 --> 00:36:13,200
Is that correct?

529
00:36:14,360 --> 00:36:17,000
Wait a moment. Let's go with "Captain Ruan", yeah.

530
00:36:17,280 --> 00:36:19,319
Change it to "Captain Ruan, Dad".

531
00:36:19,320 --> 00:36:20,679
"Happy Birthday". Correct?

532
00:36:20,680 --> 00:36:22,720
It's "Captain Ruan, Happy Birthday".

533
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:24,480
Don't mention "Dad".

534
00:36:25,320 --> 00:36:28,000
Wait a second. Maybe go with "Ruan Si Xian".

535
00:36:28,440 --> 00:36:29,720
I can't make up my mind.

536
00:36:30,840 --> 00:36:32,720
Using the full name feels a bit...

537
00:36:33,040 --> 00:36:34,040
a bit stiff.

538
00:36:34,080 --> 00:36:35,120
How about "Si Xian"?

539
00:36:35,480 --> 00:36:37,240
It's warmer but still polite.

540
00:36:37,480 --> 00:36:38,480
"Si Xian" is good.

541
00:36:38,600 --> 00:36:39,600
"Si Xian" is good.

542
00:36:39,680 --> 00:36:41,720
It implies missing her.

543
00:36:42,440 --> 00:36:43,799
- Let's go with "Si Xian". - Okay.

544
00:36:43,800 --> 00:36:45,400
Please pick it up on time.

545
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:49,000
He finally decided.

546
00:36:49,600 --> 00:36:50,880
- Si Xian? - Si Xian.

547
00:37:19,120 --> 00:37:21,440
Please come again.

548
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:24,760
Welcome.

549
00:37:24,880 --> 00:37:26,480
Hello, sir. I'm here to pick up my cake.

550
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:28,359
Could you please give me...

551
00:37:28,360 --> 00:37:30,040
the last four digits of your phone number?

552
00:37:30,120 --> 00:37:31,640
The last four digits are 4933.

553
00:37:31,800 --> 00:37:34,280
And the cake says, "Si Xian, Happy Birthday".

554
00:37:34,560 --> 00:37:36,200
"Don't Mention Dad".

555
00:37:36,920 --> 00:37:37,920
Dad?

556
00:37:38,480 --> 00:37:40,840
No, it's just "Si Xian, Happy Birthday".

557
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:43,119
Sir, when we spoke on the phone,

558
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:44,120
you were very clear.

559
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:46,160
"Si Xian, Happy Birthday".

560
00:37:46,240 --> 00:37:47,680
"Don't Mention Dad".

561
00:37:47,880 --> 00:37:48,880
No. What?

562
00:37:48,881 --> 00:37:49,919
What dad? What mom?

563
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:51,359
- I just said "Si Xian". - There's no mistake.

564
00:37:51,360 --> 00:37:52,760
There's absolutely no mistake.

565
00:37:53,080 --> 00:37:54,479
These three cakes...

566
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:55,760
are all for Ruan Si Xian.

567
00:37:56,200 --> 00:37:57,919
And the writing on the cakes...

568
00:37:57,920 --> 00:37:59,720
has been confirmed one by one.

569
00:37:59,960 --> 00:38:00,960
This one...

570
00:38:01,200 --> 00:38:02,439
is your cake.

571
00:38:02,440 --> 00:38:05,280
- This one? - "Si Xian, Happy Birthday".

572
00:38:05,600 --> 00:38:07,360
"Don't Mention Dad".

573
00:38:07,640 --> 00:38:09,320
It's written clearly on there.

574
00:38:15,280 --> 00:38:16,680
How long will it take to change it?

575
00:38:17,160 --> 00:38:18,160
Half an hour.

576
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:35,880
What's wrong with people?

577
00:38:37,280 --> 00:38:38,919
Bro, the weather forecast is so accurate.

578
00:38:38,920 --> 00:38:41,280
- It started raining just like that. - Why are you so free?

579
00:38:41,880 --> 00:38:44,080
Whatever. They're all for Ruan Si Xian anyway.

580
00:38:44,400 --> 00:38:45,639
Hurry up and change that transparent box...

581
00:38:45,640 --> 00:38:46,999
to an opaque one for me, okay?

582
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:48,440
Don't let anyone see it. Hurry up.

583
00:39:14,840 --> 00:39:15,920
There are no parking spots.

584
00:39:16,560 --> 00:39:17,759
It's fine. I'll just park here for now.

585
00:39:17,760 --> 00:39:19,520
- We'll pick it up and be right out. - Okay.

586
00:39:53,880 --> 00:39:54,880
Let's go.

587
00:39:58,080 --> 00:39:59,160
Whose car is this?

588
00:39:59,280 --> 00:40:00,280
Why is it parked here?

589
00:40:03,120 --> 00:40:04,120
Let's go.

590
00:40:07,080 --> 00:40:08,639
The cake!

591
00:40:08,640 --> 00:40:10,319
- What should we do? - It's okay.

592
00:40:10,320 --> 00:40:11,919
- It's okay. - Oh no! Where are my keys?

593
00:40:11,920 --> 00:40:12,920
The keys...

594
00:40:16,200 --> 00:40:17,440
- What should we do? - This...

595
00:40:18,200 --> 00:40:19,280
Try to fish them out.

596
00:40:21,360 --> 00:40:23,239
- I can't reach them. - What should we do?

597
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:24,240
Look. Take that.

598
00:40:24,241 --> 00:40:25,321
- Try it with that. - This?

599
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:26,600
I'll try.

600
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:28,000
Here.

601
00:40:28,001 --> 00:40:29,079
A little to the left.

602
00:40:29,080 --> 00:40:30,640
- Left. - Oh my gosh.

603
00:40:31,200 --> 00:40:32,240
Xiao Zhen!

604
00:40:32,440 --> 00:40:33,440
Your car!

605
00:40:36,360 --> 00:40:37,720
It's being towed! Hurry, let's go!

606
00:40:43,440 --> 00:40:45,160
You're all dressed up. Who are you meeting?

607
00:40:45,720 --> 00:40:46,840
You scared me.

608
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:48,560
Why didn't you make a sound?

609
00:40:49,600 --> 00:40:50,600
I'm meeting a friend.
A man or a woman?

610
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:52,840
It's none of your business.

611
00:40:54,440 --> 00:40:56,040
I'm just concerned about my subordinate.

612
00:40:57,200 --> 00:40:58,200
A man.

613
00:41:01,760 --> 00:41:02,760
Will you be back tonight?

614
00:41:05,120 --> 00:41:06,120
No.
Then do you need a ride?

615
00:41:08,120 --> 00:41:09,120
Are you sure?

616
00:41:09,240 --> 00:41:10,359
I'm quite curious to know...

617
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:11,360
who this friend is...

618
00:41:12,440 --> 00:41:13,840
who managed to get a dinner date...

619
00:41:14,080 --> 00:41:15,160
with Ms. Ruan today.

620
00:41:19,960 --> 00:41:20,960
Drive.

621
00:41:28,240 --> 00:41:30,239
Hello, Xiao Zhen. It's hard to get a taxi there.

622
00:41:30,240 --> 00:41:31,240
I'm on my way.

623
00:41:31,720 --> 00:41:32,720
What?

624
00:41:32,880 --> 00:41:34,080
You're already on your way?

625
00:41:35,400 --> 00:41:36,400
Well,

626
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:38,760
there has been a change of plans on our end.

627
00:41:39,040 --> 00:41:41,360
How about you find a place to walk around when you arrive?

628
00:41:41,520 --> 00:41:42,760
Things here won't be settled...

629
00:41:42,840 --> 00:41:43,840
anytime soon.

630
00:41:44,840 --> 00:41:45,920
Are you standing me up?

631
00:41:47,320 --> 00:41:49,760
You could say that.

632
00:41:50,200 --> 00:41:52,000
It's a bit hard to explain.

633
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:53,440
I'm really sorry.
Fine, it's okay.

634
00:41:55,240 --> 00:41:57,256
I don't have a habit of celebrating my birthday anyway.

635
00:41:57,280 --> 00:41:58,880
Go take care of your business first.

636
00:41:59,200 --> 00:42:00,416
I'll just look around on my own.

637
00:42:00,440 --> 00:42:01,440
All right, okay.

638
00:42:04,200 --> 00:42:05,200
What should we do?

639
00:42:05,600 --> 00:42:06,920
Is this cake still usable?

640
00:42:17,320 --> 00:42:18,320
Navigation ended.

641
00:42:18,800 --> 00:42:20,279
- Thank you. - What are you doing?

642
00:42:20,280 --> 00:42:21,280
Go home with me.

643
00:42:30,200 --> 00:42:31,200
Here.

644
00:42:35,320 --> 00:42:36,480
It really is a shame.

645
00:42:37,120 --> 00:42:38,720
You put so much effort into this outfit.

646
00:42:38,800 --> 00:42:40,480
I'm the only one who gets to see it today.

647
00:42:46,200 --> 00:42:47,280
We're not ordering takeout?

648
00:42:48,320 --> 00:42:49,320
No.

649
00:42:51,200 --> 00:42:52,200
What do you want to eat?

650
00:42:54,440 --> 00:42:56,440
Can you make a Manchu-Han Imperial Feast?

651
00:42:57,120 --> 00:42:58,176
You have quite an appetite.

652
00:42:58,200 --> 00:42:59,240
And even bigger ambitions.

653
00:43:04,680 --> 00:43:06,120
Longevity noodles. Do you want some?

654
00:43:08,320 --> 00:43:09,920
How did you know it's my birthday today?

655
00:43:10,600 --> 00:43:11,880
I've read your resume.

656
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:15,480
Does the boss...

657
00:43:15,600 --> 00:43:16,600
treat every employee...
with such thoughtfulness?

658
00:43:17,720 --> 00:43:19,456
I think you're asking what you already know.

659
00:43:19,480 --> 00:43:20,759
If I had to make longevity noodles...

660
00:43:20,760 --> 00:43:22,440
for every employee on their birthday,

661
00:43:23,160 --> 00:43:24,560
would I be an executive...

662
00:43:25,240 --> 00:43:26,240
or an executive chef?

663
00:43:48,400 --> 00:43:53,320
(Departing Ep. 11 for Ep. 12)
